    "body": "EICMA 2026 • Honda Africa Twin Gets Biggest Refresh in a Decade, They Now Call It CRF1150L\nThe US-Built 2027 Subaru Ascent Touring Is a 150-Vehicle Limited Edition in Japan\n7 photos\nPhoto: Subaru\nSubaru has decided to bring the Ascent to Japan. The idea came in June 2026, when the manufacturer announced that Indiana-built Ascents may be exported to Subaru's domestic market to leverage a certification system implemented by the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport, and Tourism. How come?\nYou can blame Trump's incredibly polarizing trade policy, prompted by the longstanding US trade deficit with Japan. The prez argued that Japanese regulations and certification requirements made it difficult for American manufacturers to compete in the Japanese market, but truth be told, most American vehicles simply are viewed as subpar by Japanese motorists.\nUnder a framework agreement that was subsequently implemented through an executive order in September 2025, the lesser partner agreed to make it easier for American-built vehicles to enter its market. Japan changed its certification rules in February 2026, enabling Toyota, Nissan, and Subaru to send a bunch of left-hand-drive American vehicles there, including the Tundra pickup truck.\nToyota and Nissan actually published quality-related warnings on their Japanese websites, acknowledging that US-built models may exhibit both paint and fit-and-finish characteristics that differ from Japanese domestic market automotive quality standards. Ouchie, for sure! Subject vehicles include the aforementioned Toyota Tundra half-ton pickup, the Highlander, and the Nissan Murano.\nThe Ascent three-row sport utility vehicle is Subaru's first model introduced under the new US-built vehicle certification system. These three Japanese automakers are joined by Honda, which is bringing the Acura Integra Type S and Honda Passport TrailSport Elite to Japanese customers in relatively limited numbers.\nPhoto: Subaru Limited to 150 vehicles, the Japanese-market Ascent comes in Touring specification with a retail price of 7,700,000 yen. That means 48,460 dollars at current exchange rates, which is less than what you have to pay in the United States of America. For reference, the 2027 model carries an MSRP of $51,165 as of this writing, and that's before destination charge, other taxes, and options.\nOnly available with seven rather than eight seats, the Ascent Touring is heading to Japan with a bit of a problem. The Japanese website lists a warning that concerns driver-assistance goodies, namely the EyeSight system. Subaru explicitly states that said EyeSight system was developed specifically for right-hand traffic, which is why it may not perform as intended on Japanese roads.\nBecause it's a seven-seat configuration, the Ascent Touring comes with two individual captain's chairs for the second row instead of a three-person bench seat. Folding both rear rows, the flat cargo floor of the mid-sized crossover extends more than 2 meters (78.7 inches) from the tailgate opening to the front seats, making the 2027 Subaru Ascent Touring useful beyond the school run.\nTipping the scales at 2,060 kilograms (4,542 pounds), the Japanese model carries 73 liters (19.3 gallons) of dinosaur juice in the fuel tank. Its 2.4-liter turbocharged four-cylinder boxer develops 194 kilowatts at 5,600 revolutions per minute and 375 Newton-meters at 2,000 to 4,800 revolutions per minute, figures that can be alternatively read as 260 mechanical ponies and 277 pound-feet.\nBrown Nappa leather, 14-speaker Harman Kardon audio, ventilated front seats, Symmetrical All-Wheel Drive, and X-MODE are only a few highlights. This 150-vehicle production run is limited to three paint colors. Crystal White Pearl adds 33,000 yen to the final price, while Magnetite Gray Metallic and Daybreak Blue Pearl are no-cost options. All 150 units are offered through a lottery. View this post on Instagram A post shared by 株式会社SUBARU (@subaru.jp)\nVia // Subaru Japan\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more stories from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\n2027 Subaru Ascent Subaru Ascent Subaru Japan SUV\nDownload: 2027 Subaru Ascent Touring for Japan (PDF)\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT Honda Is Recalling the S2000 Roadster for Fuel Flange Joint Leak Risk",
